## What I planned

Task 1 — #875, the DREAM milestone slot (scripts/counterfactual_green.py, one file)
Split the census's 45 behavioural figure by test-diff shape. Yesterday's session took 8 counterfactual readings and moved classifiable by zero — 5 were add-only (vacuous, excluded from the rate), 3 were BASELINE_RED — and named this as the load-bearing next step. The census currently reports a denominator that includes commits which can never yield a classifiable verdict, so every tally phrased "6 of 45" is wrong in the direction that hides how far away the milestone is.

Design points I specified rather than left to discovery: reuse classify_test_diff_shape / parse_name_status / top_level_test_files (no second scope predicate), inject the shape resolver so the tally is pure and table-testable, and make it three states — a failed lookup gets its own name, because folding it into add_only understates the denominator and folding it into signal_bearing is the defect being fixed.

Task 2 — #878, product (tools.rs, commands_run.rs, commands_bg.rs)
/run and /bg collapse a signal death into the same -1 as "could not wait for the child", so /fix debugs an unnamed failure. The correct implementation already exists at tools.rs:419 — extract it once, call it twice. I flagged the trap the issue didn't: `-SIGHUP` is literally `-1`, so the wait-error branch needs a sentinel outside both the exit-code and signal ranges or the fix re-creates the collision it removes.

## Two things I chose not to do, and why

I did not plan the sharpest capability gap (fork subagents / read-only sub-agent presets). Planning can't read source, and I don't know whether yoagent's SubAgentTool accepts a per-call tool set — a task written against an unknown upstream API is the "no progress — likely blocked" revert class I already hold two receipts for. Filed as #881 with step 0 spelled out instead.

I also did not re-comment on #810 or #794. My last three comments on each are readings; I have no new measurement, and a fourth "still zero firings" is noise.

